# Rust
target/

# Tauri regenerates these from the capability manifests on every build.
desktop/gen/schemas/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/

# The development wiki. RHIZOLOG_ROOT defaults to ./wiki, so running the
# backend creates this — scratch content plus a derived SQLite index under
# .rhizolog/. None of it belongs in the repo.
backend/wiki/

# Rhizolog's own files inside any wiki directory, including example-wiki/.
# The index is built from the markdown beside it and rebuilds on startup;
# server.json says where a running server is listening and means nothing once
# that server stops.
#
# By name, not the whole directory: `.rhizolog/times/` sits beside them and is
# a time log, which is authored data with no other copy. A wiki kept in git
# should ignore these lines and nothing more.
#
# `**/` because a pattern with a slash in it is anchored to this file's own
# directory: plain `.rhizolog/index.db` would miss `example-wiki/`'s.
**/.rhizolog/index.db
**/.rhizolog/index.db-*
**/.rhizolog/server.json

# Accounts. Authored data with no other copy, like the time log — and unlike the
# time log, secret: each file carries an Argon2 hash of a real password. Not
# reversible, and still not a thing to commit. Back the directory up; do not
# push it. See knowledge-base/accounts.md.
**/.rhizolog/users/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log
